cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use legal-rag-router or its benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "legal-rag-router: deterministic citation routing and epistemic abstention for legal RAG"
abstract: >-
  An in-process pre-router for legal retrieval-augmented generation. It reads the legal citation
  in a query, checks it against an index of the statute book, and returns exactly one decision:
  a bound coordinate to retrieve from, a clarifying question, or a refusal because the cited law
  does not exist. No model, no network, deterministic.
